{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Sun</b> — Each of them stood in its station. The meaning: there is no need for the sun by day or the moon by night, for by the light of Your arrows people are able to go." "<b>For brightness</b> — The meaning is doubled."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The referent of 'them' is sun and moon from the verse; 'each of them' is masculine singular, matching both שמש and ירח."}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:04.998894569Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}